Matthias Wei� <matthiasUNDERSCOREweiss@gmx.at> wrote:
> 
> Ok, I figured out that my NULL modem cable was no NULL modem cabel.
> Meanwhile I'm getting signals from the machine but it doesn't improve my
> sitaution: To me it seems as it endlessly loops in some system check,

It may be.  Your machine should still have a "fail-safe monitor".
Usually to turn that on you need to switch postition of some jumpers
on a motherboard.  Which ones this is a particular mobo specific.
So, unless somebody with the same board will tell you details of
the procedure, you have to dig out (try Google) manuals for your
mobo.  There should be also a description how to reload a firmware
from fail-safe when a disaster, like the one you are describing,
strikes.

That is likely the best what you can do now.

   Michal


