" DiskMan" <someone@microsoft.com> wrote:

> I was wondering, is it possible to use a GeForce II card with an
> AlphaPC ? I know the Matrox line includes a special chip which allows
> the mb/pci bus to recognize the card, would this be an issue using the
> Geforce? I've heard the ATI card works and as far as I know, it
> doesn't have a special chipset or anything... Will L G
 
Most VGAs have x86 oriented bioses so initialising such a card
in non-x86 arch will be impossible. But that does not mean you won't
boot. You need vm86 emulation for VGA bios calls. X does that on
non x86 archs, so does the framebuffer. But, as with anything - YMMV.


HTH
